## Which Type of Website Should Your Small Business Build First?

With so many options, it's easy to assume you need a website with every possible feature.

You probably don't.

The best starting point depends on what you sell, how customers find you, and what you need them to do.

Here's a quick guide.

{% table %}
- Your Business Goal
- Website Type to Consider
---
- Sell physical products online
- Ecommerce store
---
- Showcase creative work
- Portfolio website
---
- Receive service enquiries
- Business website with a contact form
---
- Accept appointments
- Booking website
---
- Display available properties
- Property listing website
---
- Promote a restaurant or food business
- Menu and ordering website
---
- Sell digital products
- Digital product website
---
- Build professional credibility
- Personal website or digital business card
---
- Attract students or parents
- Educational website
---
- Present completed projects
- Portfolio or project showcase website
{% /table %}

Start with the features that directly support your main goal.

You can add more functionality as your business grows and you learn what your customers actually need.

## How Much Does It Cost to Build a Small Business Website in Nigeria?

The cost depends on the website type, design requirements, content, integrations, and the provider you choose.

A simple landing page will generally require less work than a custom ecommerce store or a booking platform with advanced functionality.

You may also need to budget for domain registration, hosting, business email, paid tools, maintenance, or payment processing.

Before requesting a quote, decide what the website needs to achieve and which features are essential for launch.

Ask the developer to explain what is included in the price, what you will need to provide, and whether any recurring charges apply.

For a more detailed breakdown, read our guide to [how much a website costs in Nigeria](/articles/how-much-does-a-website-cost-in-nigeria).

## How Can You Make Your Small Business Website Effective?

Choosing the right type of website is only the beginning. How you present your business matters too.

### Make Your Offer Clear

Visitors should quickly understand what you sell, who you serve, and how to take the next step.

Avoid vague headlines that sound impressive but do not explain what the business actually does.

### Make It Easy to Contact You

Provide clear contact options, such as a contact form, business email, phone number, or WhatsApp link where appropriate.

Do not make visitors search through several pages to find out how to reach you.

### Use Relevant Images

Use images that accurately represent your products, services, team, or completed work.

Good visuals help visitors understand what you offer, but they should not replace useful information.

### Make It Work on Mobile

Many visitors may access your website using a phone. Text, buttons, images, forms, and navigation should remain easy to use on smaller screens.

### Build Trust

Provide accurate business information, clear policies where relevant, genuine testimonials, and examples of your work.

Never invent reviews or make claims you cannot support.

### Consider Search Visibility

Use descriptive page titles, helpful content, relevant headings, and clear URLs.

Create pages that answer the questions your potential customers are likely to search for. Technical setup also matters, but SEO is an ongoing effort rather than a one-time guarantee of rankings.

### Give Visitors a Clear Next Step

Depending on your business, that might mean placing an order, requesting a quote, booking a consultation, viewing your portfolio, or contacting you.

Make the next step easy to understand.

## Final Thoughts

There are many ways a small business in Nigeria can use a website. The right choice depends on what you offer and what you want your customers to do.

A fashion vendor may benefit from an online store. A photographer may need a portfolio. A consultant may need a professional website that explains their services. A small business owner who mainly needs a credible online presence may be able to start with a simple website.

You don't have to build everything at once.

Start with a clear goal, choose the features that support it, and improve the website as your business develops.

